      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:climate_engine",
      "title": "Climate Engine",
      "text": "Changes the air's carbon dioxide and aerosols, and with them how much heat the world keeps: enough to bring rain, clear the sky, or grow ice.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 2$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the carbon dioxide and the aerosols. Radiative forcing \u0394F = 5.35 ln(C/280 ppm) W/m\u00b2, less what the aerosols reflect; the world warms by about 0.8 K for each W/m\u00b2. Warmer air holds more water: rain, then storms. Colder grows ice. The weather recipes set the weather (the whole world's) when they finish."
    },
